        "comments": "The assembly daPauTome1.hap1.1 is based on 64x PacBio data and Arima2 Hi-C data generated by the Darwin Tree of Life Project\n(https://www.darwintreeoflife.org/). The assembly process included the following sequence of steps: initial PacBio assembly generation with Hifiasm in Hi-C integrated assembly mode, and Hi-C based scaffolding with YaHS. The mitochondrial and chloroplast genomes were assembled using OATK. Finally, each haplotype assembly was analysed and manually improved using TreeVal. Chromosome-scale scaffolds confirmed by the Hi-C data have been named in order of size. This genome has been assembled using PacBio and HiC data and phased. The result is two curated haplotypes. A haplotypic inversion was observed in the region on chromosome 1 (3.6-5.0 Mbp) and chromosome 7 (9.7-10.8 Mbp). The exact order and orientation of the contigs on chromosome 1 (12.2 - 13.1 Mbp), chromosome 11 (13.3 - 13.8 Mbp), chromosome 12 (8.2 - 8.9 Mbp) and chromosome 14 (0 - 6.1, 9.8-10.6 Mbp) are unknown.",
